'''Kuromi''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that could be obtained from the [[Nebaaru-kun and Nyanpazuru Collaboration Event|Nebaaru-kun and Nyanpazuru Collaboration]] [[Cat Capsule#Collaboration Event Capsule|Event Cat Capsule]]. It was added in [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 264
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Kuromi
|name2 = Kuromi and Cats
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kuromi and Cats''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit could be compared to [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]] and [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Li'l Gau]] as an [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]] meatshield, but what separates Kuromi from the other two is that this cat was designed to also be an attacker. As with most collab units, better alternatives are everywhere, and Kuromi is outclassed by nearly everything under the sun. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] is the main contender here, but he is far from the only option. There's also [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]], [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], and so many more. All of them work better simply because they'll do more damage than this unit will ever be able to against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies, and even non-Dark enemies.

As a meatshield, even with Strong Against, Kuromi has the same issues as other failing meatshields, those being low health, poor spammability and a somewhat high cost. Given how much damage Dark enemies do, and how using [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] provides a better defense, even without Nono or Li'l Gau, sets in stone how poor of a unit Kuromi is. Additionaly, Bombercat can't get Kuromi working either, as it's unable to knockback enemies quickly. The only way this Cat can serve you is to up your [[User Rank]]. At least he's better than [[Dragon League Swordsman (Rare Cat)|Dragon League Swordsman]], a worse anti-Dark meatshield, but that's it.

